Suspend/resume (and USB re-enumeration / daemon restarts in general) makes
the first VerifyStart after wake fail with NoReply, ClaimDevice,
NoEnrolledPrints or NoSuchDevice while the device is still settling. Only
ClaimDevice was retried; anything else left the lock session without working
fingerprint until re-lock. Poll transient failures with backoff instead, and
re-arm silently-dead verifications via a watchdog.

Bounded (16 x 500ms) so a genuinely print-less setup still gives up and
falls back to password exactly like before. Existing test contracts are kept:
disconnect still does not re-arm, foreign claims are left alone.

Upstream: github:noctalia-dev/noctalia (cachix), rev 4237bc28.
Local carry until upstream handles more than ClaimDevice.

